.TH DTOPEN 1 "2026-11-22" "Amiga UNIX add-on" "CDE"
.SH NAME
dtopen, dtopen_image, dtopen_pdf, dtopen_ps, dtopen_video \- open a file in a helper program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dtopen_image
.I file
.br
.B dtopen_pdf
.I file
.br
.B dtopen_ps
.I file
.br
.B dtopen_video
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dtopen
is one script under five names; the name it is called by says what the
file is.
The desktop's actions call it to open a file of a type CDE has no viewer
for: it runs the first viewer of a list that it finds on the
.BR PATH ,
and shows an error dialog naming the list when it finds none.
.TP 16
.B dtopen_image
images: xv, display, gimp
.TP
.B dtopen_pdf
PDF documents: okular, xpdf
.TP
.B dtopen_ps
PostScript documents: mgv, gv
.TP
.B dtopen_video
video: vlc, ffplay
.PP
Called as
.B dtopen
or any other name, it shows an error dialog listing the four names.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP 16
.B DTOPEN_VIMAGE
.PD 0
.TP
.B DTOPEN_VPDF
.TP
.B DTOPEN_VPS
.TP
.B DTOPEN_VVIDEO
.PD
a space-separated list of viewers that replaces the default list of that
name.
.SH NOTES
None of the default viewers is part of Amiga UNIX; set the variables to
viewers that are installed.
The error dialog is drawn by
.BR dterror.ds (1),
which needs
.BR dtksh ,
not yet part of this package; without it the error goes unseen.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dtaction (1),
.BR dterror.ds (1)
